  cfg = the config (ref = well-resolved reference, rapid = shipped rapid preset). L0 = the outer scale [m] ('inf' is infinite).
  scr = screens. p10, p5, p1 = the SMF loss EXCEEDED 10, 5, 1 percent of the time. d_p5 and d_p1 are the FADE DEPTH pX - p50 [dB].
  pt_p5, pt_p1 = the POINT irradiance fade -10 log10(I/<I>) exceeded 5 and 1 percent of the time [dB]. s2_I = the point index.
  s2_P = the aperture index of the 700 mm bucket. It is strongly averaged and INSENSITIVE: read it as a footnote only.
  s/tr = the mean stored wall time of one trial [s]. The +- values are 68 % bootstrap half-widths (1000 resamples).

